<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.8.5: Interpreting Average Rates of Change with Real-World Examples</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00977</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.8.5: Interpreting Average Rates of Change with Real-World Examples</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2f89a8be-03f2-4a2c-896c-6599eb28da4f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para><figure><media alt="A graph. "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1903c3abc2af4c6a8ec0ea2c81f2b371a971b2b3"/></media></figure></para>
<para> The graph above shows the population of a city from 1900 to 2000. Use the graph to answer questions 1 - 5.</para>


  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="1" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is the average rate of change of the population between 1930 and 1950? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> About 250 people per year. The population was 40,000 in 1930 and about 45,000 in 1950, an increase of 5,000 people over 20 years, which equals 250 people per year.</para>


  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1930 to 1940.</item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Positive</para>
  </list>
  
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1950 to 1970.</item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Negative</para>
  </list>
  
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1930 to 1970.</item>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Negative</para>
  </list>
  
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
      <item>What is the average rate of change of the population between 1930 and 1950? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</item>
    </list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> About 250 people per year. The population was 40,000 in 1930 and about 45,000 in 1950, an increase of 5,000 people over 20 years, which equals 250 people per year.</para>
  
</list></section>
